  volume={61},
  number={10},
  pages={5396-5408},
  abstract={This article presents a 2.4 GHz receiver with a third-harmonic time-interleaved passive mixer and reconfigurable analog finite-impulse-response (AFIR) filter. To improve linearity while maintaining low power consumption, a 6-path third-harmonic time-interleaved mixer with a 6-phase non-overlapping local oscillator (LO) is proposed, employing capacitive stacking and charge sharing techniques to enhance in-band gain and out-of-band (OOB) rejection. As the LO frequency is 1/3 of the RF frequency, the power consumption of the LO buffer can be significantly reduced without sacrificing the key RF performance. In addition, a reconfigurable-bandwidth AFIR filter is proposed to further enhance the adjacent channel rejection (ACR). The receiver is fabricated in a 40 nm CMOS technology with an active area of 0.06 mm2. The total power consumption is  $415~\mu $ W, of which the LO generator consumes  $121~\mu $ W. The proposed receiver achieves a 26.5 dBm OOB IIP3, a 5.1 dB noise figure (NF), a 61 dB ACR, and an 80 dB spurious-free dynamic range (SFDR).},
