  abstract={This article presents a 12-bit, 1-GS/s SAR-assisted pipelined ADC implemented in 28-nm CMOS featuring accurate residue amplification (RA) with low gain variation. A dual-path residue amplifier embeds an open-loop gain-error-cancellation path within the closed-loop amplification path, providing accurate gain and robust gain stability without additional timing or power overhead. Furthermore, a partially look-ahead parallel quantization technique removes the quantization delay from the critical timing path, effectively extending the RA time. Fabricated in a 28-nm CMOS process, the prototype ADC achieves a measured SNDR of 59.9 dB and an SFDR of 74.8 dB at 1 GS/s with a Nyquist input. It consumes 9.63 mW, corresponding to a FoMW of 11.9 fJ/conversion-step and a FoMS of 167.1 dB.},
